 {
 	char *acdbdata, *dsp_libs, *sns_cfg, *sns_reg, *sns_reg_config, *socinfo;
@@ -160,13 +202,7 @@ struct hexagonfs_dirent *construct_root_dir(const char *prefix, const char *dsp)
 	 * Some platforms need this in / and some need it in /mnt/vendor. Form
 	 * a hard link between both locations.
 	 */
-	persist_dir = hfs_mkdir("persist", 1,
-				hfs_mkdir("sensors", 1,
-					hfs_mkdir("registry", 1,
-						hfs_map("registry", sns_reg)
-					)
-				)
-		      );
+	persist_dir = build_persist_dir(prefix, sns_reg);
 
 	/*
 	 * Some platforms need vendor in / and some need it in /system. Form

From 40e50412812adce9dddc2be9a4510ebce05eef89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fady <me@fadyackad.dev>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:09:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] hexagonrpcd: fix descriptor lifetimes and the write paths
 added for the registry

hexagonfs_openat hands out a second file number when a name's directory part resolves to an already-assigned descriptor (".", "..", "/"), so the close in create/unlink/rename freed one still held elsewhere; hexagonfs_close now destroys only on the last reference, and fastrpc_apps_std_deinit closes descendants before the root. mapped_or_empty pointed write and truncate at implementations that dereference a NULL context for an absent directory. outbufs_calculate_size padded zero-length buffers outbufs_encode never writes, and alloc_outbufs4 did not skip the method id extended methods carry in the first primitive word. A '+' mode no longer implies O_CREAT and falls back to a read-only open on an unwritable tree, stat reports the write bit only when the backing file has it, mapped writes loop until done, and the persist layout is probed at DIR/sensors/persist/registry rather than its parent.

Signed-off-by: Fady <me@fadyackad.dev>
---
